  "term": "molecular layer",
  "definition": "The molecular layer is a layer of the dentate gyrus where asymmetric, likely excitatory, synaptic contacts are found. In this source it includes an inner and outer molecular layer, with mossy fiber sprouting occurring in the inner part after injury-related seizures.",
